sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Caller as CLI / REPL / Tests
    participant API as cranelisp_frontend::lib
    participant Reader as reader.rs
    participant Mod as module_extract.rs
    participant QQ as quasiquote.rs
    participant DM as defmacro.rs
    participant ASTB as ast_builder::build_top_level
    participant ASTR as ast_builder::build_repl_input
    participant Helpers as AST helper mini-frameworks
    participant Synth as Manual synthetic Sexp builders

    Caller->>API: parse / expand / build request
    API->>Reader: source -> Vec<Sexp>
    Note over Reader: Hand-written reader is clear locally, but token-shape knowledge lives here.

    opt module forms present
        API->>Mod: extract mod/import/export/platform
        Note over Mod: super is rewritten eagerly here, so downstream code never sees a literal super import.
    end

    opt quasiquote present
        API->>QQ: expand quasiquotes
        QQ->>Synth: build synthetic macros/Sexp* forms
    end

    opt defmacro present
        API->>DM: parse defmacro / flatten begin
        DM->>Synth: synthesize match + constructor Sexps
        Note over DM,ASTB: Synthesized Sexp must match AST builder syntax expectations exactly.
    end

    alt batch program
        API->>ASTB: build_program / build_top_level
        ASTB->>Helpers: classify head symbol
        ASTB->>Helpers: parse annotations / params / types / patterns
    else REPL input
        API->>ASTR: build_repl_input(_from_sexps)
        ASTR->>Helpers: repeat top-level classification
        ASTR->>Helpers: parse annotations / params / types / patterns
    end

    Note right of ASTR: REPL and batch top-level dispatch are separate code paths, which invites drift.
    Note right of Helpers: Large ast_builder.rs mixes top-level forms, expr lowering, trait and impl lowering, types, patterns, and special cases.
    Note right of Synth: Synthetic Sexp construction exists in multiple local DSLs, increasing coupling and boilerplate.
